>The problem is, every time the user is prompted for input, there is an
>extra linefeed before and after the prompt '>'.  Ex:
>
> blather blather text output.
>
> >
>_
>^ - cursor.  Anyone know what's happening ?  I tried to wade through the
>source and f2c libraries, but it looked pretty hopeless.
>
Yes. (I wrote it). 

The first linefeed is there because I thought it looked good. The code
is in the text output routine - I think. Maybe. You are on you own here.
It is not considered a bug.

The second is there because there is no way in legal Fortran to
do otherwise!!!! However, f2c will allow it. Get into the correct
subroutine (it IS documented, you know, right there in the docs!!)
and enable the code that puts a $ (dollar sign) format descriptor
in the read statement that outputs the >. This occurs in two places.

Doug McDonald
